  m_text: 'Instruction decode begins by examining the fetched 32-bit instruction.


    The
    first checkpoint is to read the opcode, which occupies the leftmost 6 bits and
    determines what kind of instruction is being handled by the datapath.


    Once
    the opcode is confirmed, the remaining bits can be interpreted using the correct
    instruction layout.'
